From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] compstui: a page's dialog starts with its COMPROPSHEETUI's UserData as its CPSUI user data

Brother's QL label driver's own Printing preferences page reads its
context with GetCPSUIUserData as soon as its dialog procedure gets
WM_INITDIALOG, before it sets anything, and crashed on the zero we
returned. A page made from a COMPROPSHEETUI with a dialog procedure of its
own starts with that COMPROPSHEETUI's UserData; SetCPSUIUserData still
replaces it. Brother QL-800's preferences open (in the language of the
package's resource DLL: the catalog package in our corpus is the Arabic
one).

Test: test/cpsui-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_PAGEUSERDATA).
---
--- a/dlls/compstui/optitem.c
+++ b/dlls/compstui/optitem.c
@@ -1117,6 +1117,13 @@
         }
         if (page->user_proc)
         {
+            /* the caller's dialog starts with its COMPROPSHEETUI's UserData as
+             * its CPSUI user data: makers' pages read it at once
+             * (GetCPSUIUserData, Brother's label driver) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PAGEUSERDATA
+            if (!GetPropW( hwnd, L"__wine_cpsui_user_data" ))
+                SetPropW( hwnd, L"__wine_cpsui_user_data", (HANDLE)page->cp->ui->UserData );
+#endif
             /* the caller's procedure sees the PSPINFO right after the PROPSHEETPAGE */
             psp->dwSize -= sizeof(*extra);
             ret = page->user_proc( hwnd, msg, wparam, lparam );
